With over thirty years of experience in the BDSM lifestyle, in and out of local scene
communities, Norm has been able to intentionally connect, negotiate, and explore with
a number of partners, many of whom have been quite new to understanding and connecting
with their own submission. Informed consent has always been a foundational concept for
him, from well before his own entry into the BDSM community.

Over the last two years he has found a passion for assisting the exploration of self and
submission in newer submissives. This manifests as an intent to help them discover just
what submission means to them as well as how to integrate it into their lives. He is slowly
trying to transform this knowledge into a written guidebook, with the aim to more broadly
help people to avoid falling into common problems that leave them feeling hurt, taken
advantage of, exploited, or abused.

More broadly he has a deep appreciation of the complicated way that societal conditioning,
familial expectations, and the diverse standards of acceptable sexual behavior can really
inhibit a solid relationship with one's own sexuality. 





